Start at `docs/incidents/incident-001.md` and the fixed telemetry window, not a
random source file. Datadog and generated telemetry are read-only. Every claim
must carry the applicable request ID, absolute window, monitor ID,
release/version marker, and file citation. After establishing runtime evidence,
proceed autonomously with reversible local remediation, including RabbitMQ
retry-policy edits, tests, commits, pushes, and draft PRs. Do not deploy to
production, merge, or send externally unless the operator explicitly requests
that action. Slack/Jira is draft/sandbox unless a destination is named and
authorized; never customer production. Preserve Week 1 migration assets and the
permanent `demo-reset` protection files.
